  "content": {
    "title": "How does NBA Play-In Tournament work? Format, bracket and schedule",
    "text": "Updated April 3, 2026, 8:07 a.m. ETThe 2026 NBA playoff picture is coming into focus as the regular season winds down. While the top teams have already secured their postseason berths, others are still fighting for position in the final stretch, with some on the brink of elimination and clinging to their last shot at the play-in tournament.Introduced in the 2020-21 season, the play-in tournament gives teams on the bubble a chance to play their way the postseason. The top six teams in each conference earn automatic playoff bids, while the 7th through 10th seeds compete in the play-in for each conference’s final two playoff spots.The play-in tournament consists of six games split across both conferences, scheduled for April 14–17. In each conference, the No. 7 seed hosts the No. 8 seed, with the winner clinching the No. 7 playoff spot outright.The losing teams from the first game get one more chance, facing the winner of the No. 9 vs. No. 10 matchup, with the victor earning the No. 8 seed and the losing teams going home.How does the NBA play-in tournament work?The NBA Play-In Tournament begins on Tuesday, April 14, and runs through Friday, April 17, with all six games streaming exclusively on Prime Video.The No. 7 through No. 10 seeds in each conference compete for the final two playoff spots, while the top six seeds in each conference have already secured automatic bids.The NBA Playoffs tip off Saturday, April 18, with 16 teams, eight per conference, battling through a best-of-seven bracket.Game 1 of the NBA Finals is set for Wednesday, June 3, on ABC.NBA Play-In Tournament bracketThe NBA play-in tournament standings after games played on April 2:Western Conference(7) Phoenix Suns vs. (8) Portland Trail Blazers(9) LA Clippers vs. (10) Golden State WarriorsEastern Conference(7) Toronto Raptors vs. (8) Charlotte Hornets(9) Orlando Magic vs. (10) Miami Heat",
